>> title: Hojaldre
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, laminated, butter, dough, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería, Bakery
>> aka: hojaldre, pasta de hojaldre, pasta hojaldrada, puff pastry, laminated dough, pâte feuilletée, pate feuilletee
>> pairs-with: orejas, campechanas
>> servings: 24
>> time: 11 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — the butter has to stay a sheet rather than join the dough; once it has smeared it bakes as a hard biscuit instead of leaves

>> step: mix the détrempe, chill 30 min
Mix @all-purpose flour{3 1/2%cup}(420 g), @cold water{1%cup}(240 mL), @table salt{2%tsp}(12 g) and @melted unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(42 g) to a shaggy dough, knead it just smooth, cut a cross in the top and ~chill{30%min}.

>> step: beat the block into a square, chill 20 min
Beat @cold unsalted butter{1 1/2%cup}(340 g) with @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}(30 g) between two sheets of paper into a 6-inch square, then ~chill{20%min}.

>> step: fold the dough round the block and roll out
Fold @&(~2)détrempe{}, rolled out from the cross into four petals, over @&(~1)butter block{} to shut it in, then roll the parcel to a long rectangle three times its width.

>> step: fold in three and chill 30 min — four times
Fold @&(~1)parcel{} in three like a letter, turn it a quarter, roll it out again and ~chill{30%min} — four times in all.

>> step: rest overnight before cutting
Rest @&(~1)laminated dough{} in the #refrigerator{} ~rest{8%hr} before it is cut.
